# Scope

User requested automatic error detection and retry when using Ciel AI Router
for both Claude and Codex, with no duplicated retries. The primary fixture is
the screenshot HTTP 503 with a single SSE `overloaded_error`. The same working
tree also carries the SSE delivery recovery row/tool exercised by the menu
evidence; its final focused test sweep is recorded below.

# Implementation

- `ciel_runtime_support/transient_retry.py` owns one `ContextVar`
  request-scoped budget. Reusable provider configuration never owns mutable
  retry state; `BUDGET_CONFIG_KEY` exists only as a compatibility name and is
  never stored. Sequential requests and separate threads receive independent
  budgets.
- Structured JSON/SSE error-only verdicts; retryable statuses
  500/502/503/504/529/408, plus strict non-terminal rate-limit 429 verdicts;
  terminal, authentication, usage-limit and malformed
  bodies do not retry. Default 3 for CielAiRouter, explicit `gateway_retries=0`
  disables, count capped at 10. Wait schedule 1/2/4/8/15 s (cap 30 s) with a
  0.25 s floor and `Retry-After` honored.
- The 60 s deadline bounds attempt admission, backoff and bounded pre-output
  inspection, and each opener's socket timeout is clipped to the remaining
  time. It is not a hard wall-clock interruption: DNS resolution and a
  synchronous opener's multiple socket operations can outlast it. Streaming
  after acceptance uses the caller's normal idle-timeout contract.
- Retry gates on opening only: no replay after any downstream byte. An HTTP 200
  `text/event-stream` is inspected for at most 64 KiB / 100 ms using ready
  bytes only; the read-ahead prefix is replayed unchanged, and any delivered
  byte commits the budget.
- Exhaustion re-raises the original status, headers and body exactly. Retry
  metadata is logged and published, and a human-readable note is attached to
  the exception object (`_ciel_transient_retry_note`); it is never appended to
  the provider body.
- Messages, Responses and Chat adapters share the executor; gateway reselection
  reuses the existing overlay and spends the same budget. Legacy ambiguous
  transport and initial-stream reopen paths are disabled for CielAiRouter.
- Routed Claude launches project `CLAUDE_CODE_MAX_RETRIES=0`; direct Claude uses
  the configured count. Retry watchdog, non-streaming timeout retries and
  non-streaming fallback are disabled to avoid other replay owners. Codex
  router mode keeps request/stream retries 0; direct mode passes the configured
  request count and stream retries 0. Native direct handling is not claimed to
  cover every semantic error shape; measured boundaries are below.
- Provider options expose `CielAiRouter retries`. External events exposes
  `SSE delivery recovery` and `Recover SSE delivery now`, calling MCP
  `recover_sse_delivery`. Recovery queues a resumed restart only for the sole
  registered local client, after observable stale queued input (at least
  120 s), unpaused compaction admission and cooldown (at least 900 s). It does
  not clear histories, queues or cursors.

# Verification

## Real-loopback protocol acceptance: PASS 31/31

[protocol_acceptance.py](../../../diagnostics/cielairouter-transient-retry/harness/protocol_acceptance.py)
ran the production retry wiring against owned loopback HTTP fixtures with a
private HOME/config/cwd/temp and every inherited provider/credential variable
removed.

- Final capture: [protocol-acceptance-final-reviewed.json](../../../diagnostics/cielairouter-transient-retry/harness/protocol-acceptance-final-reviewed.json),
  label `final-reviewed`, generated 2026-10-21T19:39:15Z, Python 3.11.6,
  Windows 10.0.26200.
- Console transcript: [protocol-console.txt](evidence/protocol-console.txt),
  ending `PASS 31/31  FAIL 0`.
- Final source digest check: all 11 captured file SHA-256 digests match the
  working tree after the 429 ownership and context-recovery review fixes.
  Earlier integrated captures predate those fixes and are superseded.
- Production wiring exercised: Claude Messages opener
  (`ciel_runtime.open_provider_request_with_key_retry` built by
  `upstream_retry_context()`), native Responses
  (`ciel_runtime.provider_responses_passthrough()`), Chat
  (`ciel_runtime.provider_chat_passthrough()`), and the real
  `CielAiRouterGatewayService` + `CielAiRouterGatewayOverlay` through
  `provider_network.provider_urlopen` with the production
  `reselect_cielairouter_gateway`.

| Group | Cases | Recorded hit counts |
|---|---|---|
| Messages opener | 11 | screenshot SSE then success 2; exhausted configured 3 = 4; default unset = 4; explicit 0 = 1; HTTP 200 initial error SSE = 2; output then error = 1; malformed = 1; usage limit = 1; next request fresh budget = 8 total; remote bridge = 1; selected gateway reselect = 1 failing + 1 reselected |
| Responses | 10 | screenshot SSE then success 2; exhausted configured 3 = 4; explicit 0 = 1; HTTP 200 initial error SSE = 2; output then error = 1; malformed = 1; usage limit = 1; tool item equality = 2; remote bridge = 1; selected gateway reselect = 1 + 1 |
| Chat | 10 | screenshot SSE then success 2; exhausted configured 3 = 4; explicit 0 = 1; HTTP 200 initial error SSE = 2; output then error = 1; malformed = 1; usage limit = 1; tool equality = 2; remote bridge = 1; selected gateway reselect = 1 + 1 |

Every case checked that retries carried an identical request body, endpoint and
Authorization; tool calls/definitions were delivered exactly once; the client
saw exactly one success. The selected-gateway cases recorded route state
`gateway`, a failing first gateway, reselection to the second, the same request
body on both, and an overlay route moved to the second gateway. The passthrough
harness excludes `router_http` request-dispatch wrapping (owned by a separate
scope; covered by exact-file `RouterDispatchTests`, not by a live runtime) and
live runtime, real provider or remote gateway hosts.

Superseded captures in the same directory: `protocol-acceptance-run1.json`
(20/31) and `protocol-acceptance-run2.json` (29/31). The final and integrated
runs are the 31/31 records used above.

